# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — an Agentic Foundry workspace

Scaffolded by `npx create-agentic-workspace`. The plugin's verbs are `/foundry:*`; run
`/foundry:init` once inside a trusted Claude Code session, then `/foundry:doctor` for `DOCTOR-GREEN`.

## How work happens here

**One artifact per change: a ticket with a runnable "Done means". The platform is the gate.**
Read the plugin's `context/operating-model.md` (one page) — it is the whole model.

- Start every session on a ticket: `python3 "$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/scripts/foundry-ticket.py" start <issue>`.
- Build on a branch; run the repo's tests locally with `"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/scripts/foundry-test.sh"`
  until green; push once; one PR per ticket. Push and non-draft PRs are refused until local-green.
- Do not stop on reversible work; the Stop hook runs the ticket's `Done means`.
- Do not write specs, contracts, status reports, manifests or docs the ticket did not ask for;
  the paper guard refuses them. Proposing new governance machinery is a defect.
- Ask the operator only on an irreversible, security or authorization-adjacent fork.

## Stage mode

Stage mode: {{STAGE_MODE}}

`lean` is the norm; `scale` adds the opt-in spec lane for `security: true` work.

## Floor (never relaxed)

Branch protection + CI on `main`; security review on auth / secrets / custody / supply-chain
changes; no force-push; the operator's own walkthrough before a release is called delivered.
